        "text": "Tip #4: \u201cThe Installer Tested My Graphics\nFine, but My GUI Won\u2019t Start\u201d\nIf your Linux installation program showed you a GUI desktop saying that you were\nready to proceed with the rest of the installation, you probably expected that the\nGUI would start with no problem. Unfortunately, that doesn\u2019t always happen.\nCHAPTER 22 Ten Troubleshooting Tips 425\nIf you boot your machine for the first time and see error messages when you\u2019re\ntrying to enter the GUI automatically or when you type startx to start the GUI\nmanually, type system-config-display at a command prompt to start a program\nthat can help you fix the problem.",
